1. THE REQUIREMENT AND THE ENVELOPE
   REQ-016 (v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml), verbatim: "The solar input charges the pack through board E's LT8705A stage from a panel inside its declared window: an open-circuit voltage of at most 25 V at the panel's coldest operating temperature, the panel held at 17.6 V by the stage's input regulation, and at most 100 W into the stage."
   read: at most 25 V open circuit at the panel's coldest operating temperature; held at 17.6 V; at most 100 W into the stage;
   its acceptance: F2 and J_SOLAR rated 10 A. A series diode or a clamp in place of the panel's own open circuit: NOT admitted (the statement constrains the panel's own open circuit; D4 is judged apart under TRN-001)
   TEMPERATURE: -20 C, REQ-024's in-use minimum (-20 to +40 C ambient; pcb_envelope.yaml in_use agrees); the records settle
   REQ-016's reading there (L4-ENERGY-ARCHITECTURE.md, 'What stays INCONCLUSIVE'); the panels' -40 C ratings are information.
   SESSION: with no irradiance the cells sit at the ambient (cold-soaked); Voc answers a burst of light at once, before the cells
   warm, so the envelope puts its largest irradiance on cells still at -20 C.
   IRRADIANCE (SESSION, the check's B1): G_MAX = (1 + E) x E0, with E0 the extraterrestrial irradiance at perihelion,
   1361 W/m2 / (1 - 0.0167)^2 = 1407.6 W/m2 (physical constants, ASSUMPTION class), which no clear sky exceeds on a plane facing the sun,
   and E the read source's cloud enhancement (v2/vendor/solar/irradiance-enhancement-sources-2026-10-02.md, Mol and van
   Heerwaarden 2025, ACP 25, p.1, CC BY 4.0): "In cloud fields with enough optically thin area, such as altocumulus, forward escape alone can drive areas of irradiance enhancement of over 50 % of clear-sky irradiance." E = 0.50.
   G_MAX = 2111.4 W/m2. Why so high: the enhancement is taken on the extraterrestrial irradiance, not on the clear-sky one (about
   1000 W/m2 at noon in the Netherlands: "A value of 10 W m-2 is based on 1 % of the typical order of magnitude for clear-sky irradiance around noon for Cabauw.", Mol, Knap and van Heerwaarden 2023, ESSD 15, p.8),
   so it covers the kit's in-use altitude to 3000 m (D-02c), a snow-covered ground's reflection (the same source, p.5) and
   more enhancement than the source names, with no season or weather correlation. Its cost is small: Voc grows with ln G, by
   A(T) x ln(G_MAX / 1000) = A(T) x 0.7474, with A the panel's irradiance slope (the fit's, INFERRED, until measured).
   USEFUL POWER: the stage draws its own drive and quiescent power, 42.3 mA, 1.27 W at L4-E5's raised EXTVCC (L4-E7, INFERRED there),
   from its output; at its declared 0.93 (the replay) the input must exceed 1.27 / 0.93 = 1.3656 W before any charge reaches the pack.
   owner rulings in the registry naming a panel class (a class word beside 'panel' or 'array' in one sentence): none; a1solar SELECTION.md 1 (a session's criterion) prefers folding, semi-rigid or blanket for a carried kit

