7. THE WINDOW AGAINST A PRINTED BAND (route 1's gap, INFERRED on the model)
   A band's spread is its top over its bottom (as factors on the rated Voc). A panel of a given curve shape is bounded over the
   envelope only while its band top is at most k_bound (25 V over its rated Voc at -20 C and 2111.4 W/m2) and is held only while
   its band bottom is at least k_reach (the hold's upper corner over its rated Voc at noon; the fit's Voc scales exactly with the
   voltages, checked). Both hold for some rating only while the spread is at most W = k_bound / k_reach.
   SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100                                      k_bound 1.0110; k_reach 0.9383 (18.813 V) / 0.9087 (18.221 V); W 1.0775 / 1.1126 (symmetric +-3.73 / +-5.33 %); printed spread 1.2222: WIDER than W, no rating of this shape and band fits both
   BougeRV 100W N-Type Fiberglass Foldable (SP001-BK-GRUSGA)    k_bound 1.0982; k_reach 1.0213 (18.813 V) / 0.9891 (18.221 V); W 1.0752 / 1.1102 (symmetric +-3.63 / +-5.22 %); printed spread 1.1579: WIDER than W, no rating of this shape and band fits both
   Solbian SX 156                                               k_bound 1.0016; k_reach 0.9434 (18.813 V) / 0.9137 (18.221 V); W 1.0617 / 1.0962 (symmetric +-2.99 / +-4.59 %); printed spread none printed
   BougeRV's rated row sits under its own reach floor (k_reach 1.0213 > 1): its rating, not only its band, is too low for the
   hold's upper corner.

