11. THE DECISION ON U-03 (SESSION, the check's B2): TWO ROUTES
   Route 1, a maker-bound sheet: bounded over the envelope by the printed band AND the hold inside the curve at the conditioned
   upper corner over that band AND portable:
     SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100                                      bounded NO; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
     BougeRV 100W N-Type Fiberglass Foldable (SP001-BK-GRUSGA)    bounded NO; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
     Solbian SX 156                                               bounded NO; hold yes; portable yes -> does not qualify
     on EA3's typical band (upper corner 18.221 V) instead: SPR does not qualify; BGV does not qualify; SBX does not qualify
   Route 2, a controlled unit: PANEL-ACC's contract (section 10) has a non-empty window that holds the identified panel's typical
   rows, with every condition met at the specification: yes
   U-03: CONDITIONAL DOWNSTREAM UNIT SELECTION (PANEL-ACC).
   It is not an architecture-level choice: REQ-016's window, the stage, its hold and the drafted limit stay, and the panel is
   selected downstream by measurement. It is CONDITIONAL on: a bought unit passing A-1 to A-3 by its own measurement (M1 to M4
   at the specification); L4-E7's drafted input limit applied (A-4, its 96.25 W CONDITIONAL); the unit's trace rerun (A1, A2).
   NO PHYSICAL UNIT IS ACCEPTED: none is bought or measured; the purchase and the measurement are the owner's actions (money).
   Route 1 stays open beside it: the drafts in clarification/ ask the two hold-matched makers for a warranted band (the owner
   sends them; the session contacts no outside party). REQ-016 need not change, so no owner question is raised; a series diode
   or a clamp is not a substitute (section 1).
   THE DOWNSTREAM ITEM, PANEL-ACC (Layer 6, component selection; the purchase is the owner's): accept the panel by route 1 (the
   bought revision's document, filed with its sha256, passes section 3 and section 4 over the envelope) or by route 2 (the
   identified unit passes A-1 to A-3 at the specification, section 10); in either case rerun its trace through the replay's
   section 12 and L4-E7's section 5 (A1 and A2), keep F2's and J_SOLAR's 10 A (A-3) and the 100 W on L4-E7's limit (A-4).

12. EVIDENCE CLASSES: MAKER (SunPower's sheet and guide, Solbian's sheet), MAKER-PAGE (BougeRV's page, transcribed), RECORD
    (the replay's and L4-E7's outputs, the stage's drive power), MODELED (the energy record's single-diode model and day), INFERRED
    (the irradiance slopes, the window ratios, the demonstration unit, the cell temperature at the hot end), ASSUMPTION (S0 and the
    orbit's eccentricity as physical constants; a band's voltages scaled with its currents kept; BougeRV's rows taken as STC),
    LITERATURE (the enhancement and the Cabauw quotations, CC BY 4.0), SESSION (the envelope, the 10 % sentence's reading, the
    coefficient as a fraction, the hold screen and the day's 5 % hours, the conditioned band, PANEL-ACC's unit, measurements and
    specification, the useful-power line).
